  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Answer using a spreadsheet. Andreas puts $\\$1400$ into an annuity at the end of each quarter for 5 years. The annuity pays 6.8% p.a. compounding quarterly. Give monetary answers to the nearest cent.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Andreas does not have enough in his annuity after 5 years to purchase his dream car, which retails for $\\$42\\,000$. By how much is he short?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "He has $\\$33\\,018.46$ after 5 years, so he is $\\$8981.54$ short.",
          "worked": "The quarterly interest rate is $6.8\\%\\div4=1.7\\%$, and 5 years contains 20 quarters.\n\nEnter 0 in A2 and B2. In A3 enter `=A2+1`, and in B3 enter `=B2*1.017+1400`. Fill both formulas down to 20 quarters, retaining full precision.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}V_0&=0\\\\V_{n+1}&=1.017V_n+1400\\\\V_{20}&=33018.461493\\ldots\\\\\\text{Shortfall}&=42000-33018.461493\\ldots\\\\&=\\$8981.54\\text{ (nearest cent)}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
